<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Northern Isles</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Northern Isles are the archipelagos of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orkney">Orkney</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shetland">Shetland</a> off the north coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>. Settled by Norse <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a> from the 9th century, they formed the Earldom of Orkney under Norwegian overlordship. In 1468–69 King Christian I of Denmark-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> pledged them to Scotland as security for his daughter's dowry, and they were never redeemed. Norse influence survives in their place names and dialects.</p></div>
